  "_comment": "Drills as vertices of the graph. The key is the drill's id (d1, d2, ...): assigned once, never reused, the way LeetCode numbers are; it is what \"after\" lists, make prepare and make next use. \"title\" is the DRILL header of the bank file (drills/<node>/*.py), which is how the file, its node and its TRAINS line are found, and how evidence is keyed. \"after\": [ids] - what this drill builds on; an id is a drill id, a problem number, or a node id, and the drill is not served until each is warm (kg_lib.warm). Filename order means nothing. Seeded 2026-08-31 from the bank's former filename order. \"trains\" is the list of node ids the drill evidences; it lives here, keyed by the stable id, so a node rename never touches a bank file or a solved copy.",
